k_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the typing issue\r\n\r\nThe .values() method requires a dict, which makes it rather cumbersome to type, as the type must match the full definition.\r\nhttps://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/main/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/dml.py#L947\r\n\r\nMaybe this should be typed as Mapping instead? In that case, it should probably work with an intersection of the dict types.\r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\n```python\r\nd: dict[str, Any]\r\nsa.insert(table).values(d)\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Error\r\n\r\n```\r\naiohttp_admin/backends/sqlalchemy.py:107:50: error: Argument 1 to \"values\" of \"ValuesBase\" has incompatible type \"Dict[str, Any]\"; expected\r\n\"Union[Dict[Union[str, _HasClauseElement, DMLColumnRole, SQLCoreOperations[Any]], Any], Sequence[Any]]\"  [arg-type]\r\n                stmt = sa.insert(self._table).values(params[\"data\"]).returning(*self._table.c)\r\n                                                     ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n``` \r\n\r\n### Versions\r\n\r\n- Python: 3.9\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 2.0.4\r\n- Type checker: mypy 1.0.1\r\n\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\nI think the reason it won't allow dict[str, Any] is because a function with that signature could assign non-str keys into the passed dict. With a Mapping, which is immutable, I would expect mypy to allow passing this dict.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9376/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}